# BSI IT-Grundschutz-Kompendium, Edition 2023, the publisher's own XML.
#
# One URL, because the BSI publishes the whole Kompendium as a single DocBook
# document. That is why this corpus replaced a private registry: the same text,
# from the agency that wrote it, at an address anybody can fetch.
#
# The `v=4` is load-bearing. BSI's download handler serves whatever the current
# revision of a document is when the parameter is absent, so a list without it
# would drift under the committed counts and the gate would report a corpus that
# had moved as a rule that had changed. With it pinned, a re-fetch returns the
# same 3,160,564 bytes it did on the day below.
#
# The XML is the right source rather than the PDF or the XLSX checklists. It is
# the publisher's structured original, so no-break spaces and quotation marks
# survive byte-exact, where a PDF text layer flattens spacing and a page reader
# would be inventing the evidence this gate is supposed to weigh.
#
# Frozen 2026-08-10. format: xml
#
# No second column anywhere below: the archive holds no capture of this URL,
# so this corpus is always fetched live. The `v=4` above is what makes that
# safe, and it is a stronger pin than a capture would be.

https://www.bsi.bund.de/SharedDocs/Downloads/DE/BSI/Grundschutz/IT-GS-Kompendium/XML_Kompendium_2023.xml?__blob=publicationFile&v=4
